5. DIFFERENCES & COMPARISON VS OKTA SAML FLOW
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
• Claim URI Format:                   Entra uses full WS-Federation/Microsoft XML namespace URIs
                                      (http://schemas.xmlsoap.org/... and http://schemas.microsoft.com/...)
                                      whereas Okta defaults to short unqualified names (email, role).
• Email / UPN Resolution:             Entra cloud test users without an Exchange mailbox emit user.userprincipalname
                                      (UPN) or NameID. Handled seamlessly by Sentraa AI's fallback chain.
• App Roles vs Group Claims:          Entra default group claims emit directory GUIDs (which safely default to VIEWER).
                                      Enterprise role mapping requires Entra App Roles, which emit string names in the role claim.
• Callback Processing Time:           75.8 ms (POST /api/v1/saml/entra-test-sso/callback 302).
• Errors / Warnings:                  0 SAML callback warnings or errors in server log.
